            <ArticleTitle>Pd-Catalyzed Enantio- and Regioselective Formation of Allylic Aryl Ethers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6388-6391</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03247</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A general methodology for the synthesis of enantioenriched tertiary allylic aryl ethers through Pd-catalyzed decarboxylative reactions of vinyl cyclic carbonates and phenols is presented. Switching of the regioselectivity toward the formation of linear products by a judicious choice of the ligand is also reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
